uation:\n\nc d\u2083 (14 t - d\u2081) + 9 d\u2083 (0 - (c + d\u2082)) + (-9 d\u2082 + 11 c - c d\u2081)(0 - d\u2083) = 0\n\nLet me expand each term:\n\nFirst term: c d\u2083 (14 t - d\u2081) = 14 c d\u2083 t - c d\u2083 d\u2081\n\nSecond term: 9 d\u2083 (-c - d\u2082) = -9 c d\u2083 - 9 d\u2082 d\u2083\n\nThird term: (-9 d\u2082 + 11 c - c d\u2081)( -d\u2083 ) = 9 d\u2082 d\u2083 - 11 c d\u2083 + c d\u2081 d\u2083\n\nSo combining all terms:\n\n14 c d\u2083 t - c d\u2083 d\u2081 -9 c d\u2083 -9 d\u2082 d\u2083 +9 d\u2082 d\u2083 -11 c d\u2083 +c d\u2081 d\u2083 = 0\n\nLet me simplify term by term:\n\n- The first term is 14 c d\u2083 t\n\n- The second term is -c d\u2083 d\u2081\n\n- Third term: -9 c d\u2083\n\n- Fourth term: -9 d\u2082 d\u2083\n\n- Fifth term: +9 d\u2082 d\u2083\n\n- Sixth term: -11 c d\u2083\n\n- Seventh term: +c d\u2081 d\u2083\n\nNow, let's combine like terms:\n\nFor terms with c d\u2083 t: 14 c d\u2083 t\n\nFor terms with c d\u2083 d\u2081: -c d\u2083 d\u2081 + c d\u2083 d\u2081 = 0\n\nFor terms with c d\u2083: -9 c d\u2083 -11 c d\u2083 = -20 c d\u2083\n\nFor terms with d\u2082 d\u2083: -9 d\u2082 d\u2083 +9 d\u2082 d\u2083 = 0\n\nSo after simplifying, the equation becomes:\n\n14 c d\u2083 t -20 c d\u2083 = 0\n\nFactor out 14 c d\u2083 t -20 c d\u2083 = c d\u2083 (14 t - 20) = 0\n\nAssuming c \u2260 0 and d\u2083 \u2260 0 (since otherwise the parallelepiped would be degenerate, i.e., flat in some direction), then we can divide both sides by c d\u2083:\n\n14 t - 20 = 0 \u2192 14 t = 20 \u2192 t = 20/14 = 10/7 \u2248 1.42857\n\nTherefore, the point Z is at (14 * (10/7), 0, 0) = (20, 0, 0)\n\nThus, DZ is the distance from D(0,0,0) to Z(20,0,0), which is 20 units.\n\nWait, but this seems too straightforward, and all the variables like c, d\u2081, d\u2082, d\u2083 canceled out. That's interesting. Let me check the steps again to ensure there's no mistake.\n\nWe found the normal vector, substituted the parametrization of DA into the plane equation, and