dding 100 days from the start of the next year, the total number of days is:\n      \\[\n      165 + 100 = 265 \\text{ days}\n      \\]\n\n3. We check whether 265 or 266 is divisible by 7.\n    - \\(266 \\div 7 = 38\\)\n    - Therefore, 266 is divisible by 7.\n    \n    - On the other hand, \\(265 \\div 7 = 37 \\frac{6}{7}\\)\n    - 265 is not divisible by 7.\n\n4. Since 266 is divisible by 7, the current year is a leap year (366 days).\n\n5. Knowing the current year is a leap year, the previous year was a common year.\n\n6. Next, we calculate the number of days between the 300th day of the previous year and the 200th day of the current leap year.\n    \n    - In a previous common year, the last day is the 365th day.\n    - The number of days from the 300th day of the previous common year to the end of that year is:\n      \\[\n      365 - 300 = 65 \\text{ days}\n      \\]\n    - Adding the first 200 days of the current leap year:\n      \\[\n      65 + 200 = 265 \\text{ days}\n      \\]\n\n7. Since \\( 265 = 37 \\times 7 + 6 \\), the 300th day of the previous year was exactly 265 days before the 200th day of the current year.\n\n8. The 200th day of the current year is a Sunday. Counting 6 days backwards from Sunday:\n    - \\( \\text{Sunday} - 1 day = \\text{Saturday} \\)\n    - \\( \\text{Saturday} - 1 day = \\text{Friday} \\)\n    - \\( \\text{Friday} - 1 day = \\text{Thursday} \\)\n    - \\( \\text{Thursday} - 1 day = \\text{Wednesday} \\)\n    - \\( \\text{Wednesday} - 1 day = \\text{Tuesday} \\)\n    - \\( \\text{Tuesday} - 1 day = \\text{Monday} \\)\n\n9. Therefore, the 300th day of the previous year was a Monday.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "In a right triangle \\( ABC \\) with \\( AC = 16 \\) and \\( BC = 12 \\), a circle with center at \\( B \\) and radius \\( BC \\) is drawn. A tangent to this circle is constructed parallel to the hypotenuse \\