erday, as the process turns them white.\n   - White dandelions yesterday were yellow the day before yesterday (i.e., today minus two days).\n\n4. **Calculate the Number of Yellow Dandelions Two Days Ago:**\n   - The white dandelions yesterday (14) were yellow the day before yesterday.\n   - The white dandelions today (11) were also yellow the day before yesterday.\n\n$$\n\\text{Number of yellow dandelions two days ago} = \\text{White dandelions yesterday} + \\text{White dandelions today}\n$$\n\n5. **Conclude:**\n\n$$\n\\text{Number of yellow dandelions two days ago} = 14 + 11 = 25\n$$\n\n### Conclusion:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "The famous Fibonacci sequence is defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\nF_{0}=0, F_{1}=1 \\\\\nF_{n+2}=F_{n+1}+F_{n}\n\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\n1. Let $\\varphi$ and $\\varphi'$ be the two roots of the equation $x^2 - x - 1 = 0$.\n\n$$\n\\varphi=\\frac{1+\\sqrt{5}}{2}, \\varphi^{\\prime}=\\frac{1-\\sqrt{5}}{2}\n$$\n\nShow that there exist two real numbers $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$ such that\n\n$$\nF_{n}=\\lambda \\cdot \\varphi^{n}+\\mu \\cdot \\varphi^{\\prime n}\n$$\n\nCan you generalize the result to any sequences of the type $u_{n+2} = a u_{n+1} + b u_{n}$?\n\n2. Show that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac{F_{n+1}}{F_{n}} = \\varphi\n$$\n\n3. Show the following formulas:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\n\\sum_{i=1}^{n} F_{i}^{2}=F_{n} F_{n+1} \\\\\nF_{2n-1}=F_{n}^{2} + F_{n+1}^{2} \\\\\nm \\mid n \\Rightarrow F_{m} \\mid F_{n}\n\\end{gathered}\n$$", "deepseek_reasoning": "Alright, so I need to tackle these three questions about the Fibonacci sequence. Let me start with the first one. \n\nQuestion 1 asks to show that there exist real numbers \u03bb and \u03bc such that F\u2099 = \u03bb\u03c6\u207f + \u03bc\u03c6'\u207f, where \u03c6 and \u03c6' are the roots of x\u00b2 - x - 1 = 0. Then, it wants a generalization for any sequence u\u209